      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8840145::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Single-phase CoCrFeNiTi has favorable machinability.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Single-phase CoCrFeNiTi has relatively low hardness and yield strength.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8840145::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC9744852::web::015::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The low hardness and yield strength are caused by an absence of effective dislocation-pinning sites.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dynamic recovery dominates deformation in the homogeneous solid-solution state.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The absence of obstacles permits facile dislocation glide.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9744852::web::015::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Facile glide and dynamic recovery produce low strain hardening.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A tailored thermal treatment can produce finely dispersed, submicron, coherent precipitates in CoCrFeNiTi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8840145::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Finely dispersed precipitates act as dislocation-pinning sites.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitates increase dislocation accumulation and suppress dynamic recovery.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Introducing precipitates will increase strain hardening, yield strength, and hardness.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8840145::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC9744852::web::015::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitate-modified alloy will retain good ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8840145::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive precipitation or an unsuitable precipitate distribution could reduce plasticity.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9744852::web::015::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The quantitative strengthening depends on precipitate size, volume fraction, and distribution.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9744852::web::015::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The comparison should use an as-cast homogeneous control and a precipitate-modified sample tested under identical room-temperature loading conditions.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
